Directory Permissions

Suppose you have:
drwxr-x---
The permissions apply to the directory itself, not the files inside it.

Read (r)
For a directory, r means:
Can list filenames
Example:
ls mydir
If you have r permission, you can see:
file1.txt
file2.txt
script.sh

Write (w)
For a directory, w means:
Create files
Delete files
Rename files
Example:
touch newfile.txt
rm oldfile.txt
mv a.txt b.txt
These require write permission on the directory.

Execute (x)
For a directory, x means:
Enter/traverse the directory
Example:
cd mydir
Without x:
cd mydir
